### P04: ingest and read back events
### Paste under your existing requests, below the line that defines @host.
### Ids are Guid-based (ev_3f2a...), so request 1 is named "first" and later
### requests read its id from the response: {{first.response.body.$.id}}
@host = http://localhost:5039
### 1. First time: saved -> 202 Accepted, Location: /events/ev_..., body { id, source, eventId, status, receivedAt }
# @name first
POST {{host}}/in/stripe
Webhook-Id: evt_1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "charge.succeeded", "amount": 500 }

### 2. Same webhook again -> 200 OK, SAME id as request 1 (not saved twice)
POST {{host}}/in/stripe
Webhook-Id: evt_1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "charge.succeeded", "amount": 500 }

### 3. Source in capitals -> still a repeat: 200, same id
POST {{host}}/in/STRIPE
Webhook-Id: evt_1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "charge.succeeded", "amount": 500 }

### 4. Same Webhook-Id, different source -> a NEW event: 202, a different id
POST {{host}}/in/github
Webhook-Id: evt_1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "action": "opened" }

### 5. New Webhook-Id -> 202, new id
POST {{host}}/in/stripe
Webhook-Id: evt_2
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "charge.refunded", "amount": 500 }

### 6. Read back the event from request 1 -> 200, same body as request 1
GET {{host}}/events/{{first.response.body.$.id}}

### 7. Unknown id -> 404 (problem+json)
GET {{host}}/events/ev_nope

### 8. Unknown source -> 400, errors.source
POST {{host}}/in/paypal
Webhook-Id: evt_9
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "x" }

### 9. Number as source -> 400, errors.source (Enum.IsDefined check)
POST {{host}}/in/7
Webhook-Id: evt_9
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "x" }

### 10. No Webhook-Id header -> 400, errors.webhookId
POST {{host}}/in/stripe
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "x" }

### 11. Blank Webhook-Id -> 400, errors.webhookId
POST {{host}}/in/stripe
Webhook-Id:
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "x" }

### 12. Empty body -> 400, errors.payload
POST {{host}}/in/stripe
Webhook-Id: evt_10
Content-Type: application/json

### 13. Two problems at once -> ONE 400 with both errors.source and errors.webhookId
POST {{host}}/in/paypal
Content-Type: application/json

{ "type": "x" }


### 14. 
GET {{host}}/events?source=stripe

### 15.
GET {{host}}/events
